---BitbucketServerConfig represents the configuration for a Bitbucket Server.
---@class gcp.unstable.cloudbuild_v1.BitbucketServerConfig
---@field peeredNetworkIpRange? string Immutable. IP range within the peered network. This is specified in CIDR notation with a slash and the subnet prefix size. You can optionally specify an IP address before the subnet prefix value. e.g. `192.168.0.0/29` would specify an IP range starting at 192.168.0.0 with a 29 bit prefix size. `/16` would specify a prefix size of 16 bits, with an automatically determined IP within the peered VPC. If unspecified, a value of `/24` will be used. The field only has an effect if peered_network is set.
---@field name? string Identifier. The resource name for the config.
---@field secrets? gcp.unstable.cloudbuild_v1.BitbucketServerSecrets Required. Secret Manager secrets needed by the config.
---@field sslCa? string Optional. SSL certificate to use for requests to Bitbucket Server. The format should be PEM format but the extension can be one of .pem, .cer, or .crt.
---@field peeredNetwork? string Optional. The network to be used when reaching out to the Bitbucket Server instance. The VPC network must be enabled for private service connection. This should be set if the Bitbucket Server instance is hosted on-premises and not reachable by public internet. If this field is left empty, no network peering will occur and calls to the Bitbucket Server instance will be made over the public internet. Must be in the format `projects/{project}/global/networks/{network}`, where {project} is a project number or id and {network} is the name of a VPC network in the project.
---@field webhookKey? string Output only. UUID included in webhook requests. The UUID is used to look up the corresponding config.
---@field connectedRepositories? gcp.unstable.cloudbuild_v1.BitbucketServerRepositoryIdList Output only. Connected Bitbucket Server repositories for this config.
---@field apiKey? string Required. Immutable. API Key that will be attached to webhook. Once this field has been set, it cannot be changed. If you need to change it, please create another BitbucketServerConfig.
---@field createTime? string Time when the config was created.
---@field username? string Username of the account Cloud Build will use on Bitbucket Server.
---@field hostUri? string Required. Immutable. The URI of the Bitbucket Server host. Once this field has been set, it cannot be changed. If you need to change it, please create another BitbucketServerConfig.

