---Location of the source in any accessible Git repository.
---@class gcp.unstable.cloudbuild_v1.GitSource
---@field dir? string Optional. Directory, relative to the source root, in which to run the build. This must be a relative path. If a step's `dir` is specified and is an absolute path, this value is ignored for that step's execution.
---@field revision? string Optional. The revision to fetch from the Git repository such as a branch, a tag, a commit SHA, or any Git ref. Cloud Build uses `git fetch` to fetch the revision from the Git repository; therefore make sure that the string you provide for `revision` is parsable by the command. For information on string values accepted by `git fetch`, see https://git-scm.com/docs/gitrevisions#_specifying_revisions. For information on `git fetch`, see https://git-scm.com/docs/git-fetch.
---@field url? string Required. Location of the Git repo to build. This will be used as a `git remote`, see https://git-scm.com/docs/git-remote.

---Represents a git repository as a build dependency.
---@class gcp.unstable.cloudbuild_v1.GitSourceDependency
---@field revision? string Required. The revision that we will fetch the repo at.
---@field repository? gcp.unstable.cloudbuild_v1.GitSourceRepository Required. The kind of repo (url or dev connect).
---@field fetchTags? boolean Optional. True if remote tags should be fetched too (default false). Note: when depth is 1 (default), git fetch only retrieves tags pointing to commits within the shallow boundary. Set depth to -1 to fetch all historical tags.
